XFAIL: *

When a build tool kills a command it started (a timeout, a cancelled job),
the program itself stops, rather than only the process catter put in
between.
Known failures: #138 (killing catter-proxy leaves the program running).

RUN: %e2e probe kill-child | FileCheck %s
RUN: %catter script::cdb -q -o %t.json -- %e2e probe kill-child | FileCheck %s

CHECK: PASS kill-child
